From: superslor <289523157+superslor@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 09:03:29 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 04/19] HIP GCN FA tile: read q4_0/q8_0 K/V straight into the
 shared tile

The tile kernel dequantizes a q4_0 or q8_0 cache into its shared tile (Kmic-68's loader,
via qr0n/p100-llama-cpp), so launch_fattn no longer converts the whole cache to f16 first: that staging was
1 GiB for Qwen3.5 9B and another 1 GiB for its MTP draft at 262144. On GCN for head size 256 and an even
GQA ratio: K q8_0/q4_0 with V q4_0, and K/V q8_0 (the MTP draft cache), at every token count. AMD's
np > 1 tile configs keep the whole-cache VKQ through the cross-warp combine.

MI25, Qwen3.5 9B at 21k: read 210 -> 370 t/s, write 32.4 -> 33.4 (ubatch 512 with staging -> 1024).
One token at 20k, K q8_0 / V q4_0: Qwen3.5 9B 500 -> 207 us.
GGML_CUDA_FA_TILE_Q4_0=0 turns it off.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
